@@ -5,11 +5,22 @@ Searches the audit log.
 ## Usage
 
 ```sh
-PYTHONPATH=src python -m auditlog.search --actor alice --action login
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m auditlog.search --actor alice --action login --since 2026-01-01 --limit 20 --offset 20
 ```
 
-`--sort` and `--direction` select the ordering column and direction; both default
-to a timestamp descending sort. Results are unpaginated.
+Options:
 
-Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same escaping and ordering
-rules apply to every query against the table.
+- `--actor` (required): actor to match.
+- `--action`: action to match. Omit it to match every action for the actor.
+- `--since`: only rows whose `ts` is at or after this ISO 8601 date or datetime
+  (e.g. `2026-01-31`). Invalid values are rejected.
+- `--sort`: any column of the audit table (`id`, `actor`, `action`, `target`, `ts`);
+  default `ts`.
+- `--direction`: `asc` or `desc`; default `desc`.
+- `--limit`: maximum rows returned, 1-1000; default 50.
+- `--offset`: rows to skip; default 0.
+
+Ordering has an `id` tie-breaker so `--limit`/`--offset` pages are stable.
+
+Clause building lives in `auditlog.filters`, so the same ordering and
+validation rules apply to every query against the table.
